# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SageView Production Ltd, environment
# Copy to `.env.local` (never commit that file) and fill in what you need.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The public origin of the live site.
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph tags, the sitemap and robots.txt.
# Set this before the first production deploy or those will point at the
# placeholder domain.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://www.sageviewproduction.com

# Where project enquiries are delivered.
#
# Leave this unset and the contact form will tell visitors plainly that it is
# not connected yet and to email SageView directly. It will never report a
# submission as sent when it was not.
#
# Set it to any endpoint that accepts a JSON POST, a Zapier or Make webhook,
# an n8n flow, a Slack workflow, a Google Apps Script URL, or your own handler.
# See src/lib/enquiry-delivery.ts for the payload shape and for how to swap in
# an email provider (Resend, Postmark, SendGrid, SES) instead.
# CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enquiry delivery
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nothing here is required. With no variables set, enquiries are emailed to
# the published contact address through FormSubmit, a free relay that needs no
# account, no key and no DNS. The only setup is clicking the "Activate Form"
# link it emails to that address the first time an enquiry is sent.
#
# The trade-off: enquiries, including any attached brief, pass through a third
# party. Fine for new-business enquiries, and the reason to move to Resend
# below when there is a moment.
#
# Set ENQUIRY_RELAY=off to disable the relay, after which the form tells
# visitors to email directly unless one of the routes below is configured.
#
# Set RESEND_API_KEY and every submitted enquiry is emailed to ENQUIRY_TO,
# with the uploaded brief attached and reply-to set to the sender, so replying
# from the inbox answers them directly.
#
# Setting it up, once:
#   1. Create an account at resend.com (the free tier covers 3,000 emails a
#      month, which is far beyond what an enquiry form will ever send).
#   2. Add sageviewproduction.com as a domain and publish the DNS records it
#      gives you. This is what lets mail be sent as @sageviewproduction.com
#      without landing in spam.
#   3. Create an API key and set it here, and in the Vercel project settings
#      under Environment Variables.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Where enquiries are delivered. Defaults to the published contact address.
# ENQUIRY_TO=hello@sageviewproduction.com

# The envelope sender. Must be on the domain verified above: sending as the
# visitor's own address would fail SPF and be filtered.
# ENQUIRY_FROM=SageView Website <enquiries@sageviewproduction.com>
